m No. 4:\nBuffalo County, Wisconsin \nTract B-248, aggregating 1.72 acres, \nmore or less.\nLock and Dam No. 5:\nWabasha County, Minnesota \nTracts Wa^l05, 106, 107A, 121B, 135, \nand 147, aggregating 138.30 acres] \nmore or less.\n. Buffalo County, Wisconsin\nTracts B-306A &  B, 306C, 307A, 307B, \n312, 313, 316, and 318, aggregating \n63.87 acres, more or less.\nLock and Dam No. 5A:\nWinona County, Minnesota \nTracts Wi—42, 43, 56, 57, 58, 59, 60, \n62, 63, 67, 68, 69, 70, 71, 82, 84, 85","path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/texts/cd-job-fr-originals-8331-1f6007d8f5.txt","sha256":"43f1447409552224d3ef743efda065b72fde83b237a9e76b493c42980391212a","source":{"line":365,"path":"jobs/clause-drafts/output/SOURCES.jsonl","record_sha256":"4850b2dce27b96742a305c791c568f0bd9dae65eb414f81aee70e371512c0056"}},{"first_1500_characters":"Instrument: EO:8331\nSource: https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-1940-01-27/pdf/FR-1940-01-27.pdf\nSHA-256 of the downloaded file: 1f6007d8f5be31afa625d038bf690afc749f096230fd662a5b8b46e8ea8aef5b\nLocation: 5 FR 314, PDF pages 2-3 (confidence high)\nMachine-extracted text layer of the official PDF (OCR for 1936-1994 scans). May contain recognition errors and parts of neighbouring documents on the same pages. Not an authenticated transcription: check the PDF pages.\n\n=== PDF page 2 of 8 ===\n314 FEDERAL REGISTER, Saturday, January 27, 1940\nFEDERAIÄREGISTER\n\\  I » 3 *  ¿P\nONrvtO*\nPublished daily, except Sundays, Mondays, \nand days following legal holidays by the \nDivision of th e Federal Register, The National \nArchives, pursuant to  the authority con­\ntained in th e Federal Register Act, approved \nJuly 26, 1935 (49 Stat. 500), under regula­\ntions prescribed by th e Administrative Com­\nm ittee, approved by th e President.\nThe Administrative Committee consists of \nthe Archivist or Acting Archivist, an officer \nof th e Departm ent of Justice designated by \nthe Attorney General, and the Public Printer \nor Acting Public Printer.\nThe